AB  - The public finance management and public procurement, work in close integration to achieve the policy goals & strategic development objectives. It is estimated that the size of public procurement is more than 13 trillion US dollars per year. Public procurement is continuously at risk from wastages in the process, the integrity of the process, and corruption together. The indicators of optimization are efficiency, which is related to the process, and effectiveness, which relates to the achievement of goals & objectives. Mainly, focus is given to the public procurement of civil works as it represents the main chunk of spending, but focus on goods type public procurement is also required as it is the second type on which most public spending is carried. The need is to consider the goods type in public procurement as a focal point and the factors that contribute to the efficiency of this specific type. This exploratory analysis is required because the goods type is challenging as there are different types of variety and different natures of supplies, which makes it difficult and needs a standalone approach based on its specific challenges & issues. The research approach for the issue at hand requires identifying the factors responsible for efficiency particular to the "Goods" type and then using those factors along with input from the experts to rigorous analysis approach Delphi to create a list of critical efficiency factors that are properly validated & refined so that only critical factors play a vital role in the efficiency of "Goods" type are identified & listed. The resultant critical efficiency factors particular to goods type will lead the way to an improved decision support system implementation and, most importantly, an approach most suited to the particular type of public procurement "Goods". © 2025 The Authors.
