AB  - US president Barack Obama's overreach and a continued engagement in pursuing growth and reform policies can help the Republicans improve their damaged image. Obama's victory in 2008 pushed the Republicans into recession, with Democrats holding 60 seats in the Senate and 257 seats in the House. Democrats took advantage of the corruption charges against Republicans and Iraq war debacle to unseat the latter. Obama's image has also taken a plunge post election, and the public are concerned with over government spending. Republicans need to take advantage of the situation and revive support among members of Hispanics group. Republicans can also defy the national defense policies of Obama, who has frozen defense spending at variance with American global commitments. Republicans can also present a detailed reform agenda before the public, taking up issues like simplifying the intricate US tax-code, improving the health-care system, and creating a modern-day regulatory system for financial institutions.
